<article>
	<h1><span>Storefront: Product Meta Info</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sub-menu">Sub-menu Links</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This screen lists store products. Opening a product here leads to its <strong>Product Meta Info</strong>
			screen, which holds the options that belong to the product's type.</p>
		<p>Only products of the <strong>Software Download</strong> type have such options. For any other product,
			the editing screen reports &quot;No meta for this product&quot;.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Checkbox</dt>
			<dd>Check this box to select one or more items. To select all items, check the box in the column heading.
				After one or more boxes are checked, click a toolbar button to take an action on the selected item or
				items. If multiple items are checked and you press Edit, the first item will be opened for
				editing.</dd>

			<dt>Title</dt>
			<dd>The name of the product. If you may edit products, the name links to the product's
				<strong>Product Meta Info</strong> screen.</dd>

			<dt>Type</dt>
			<dd>The name of the product's type.</dd>

			<dt>Published</dt>
			<dd>Shows whether the product is Published, Unpublished or Trashed.</dd>

			<dt>Access</dt>
			<dd>The product's access level, shown as a number.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Options</dt>
			<dd>Opens the Storefront configuration options in a pop-up window.</dd>

			<dt>Publish</dt>
			<dd>This screen has no publish task, so pressing it only shows the list again.</dd>

			<dt>Unpublish</dt>
			<dd>This screen has no unpublish task, so pressing it only shows the list again.</dd>

			<dt>New</dt>
			<dd>Runs the same task as Edit, with no product selected.</dd>

			<dt>Edit</dt>
			<dd>Opens the <strong>Product Meta Info</strong> screen for the selected product. If more than one product
				is selected, only the first one will be opened.</dd>

			<dt>Delete</dt>
			<dd>This screen has no delete task, so pressing it only shows the list again.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="sub-menu">
		<h2><span>Sub-menu Links</span></h2>
		<p>At the top left, you will see sub-menu options. The links are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Products</dt>
			<dt>Collections</dt>
			<dt>Option Groups</dt>
		</dl>
	</section>
</article>
